  2a. AprilTag marker images - REGENERATED, BSD-2-Clause
      Files     : third_party/ir_2526/ir_base/models/artag/**
      Base data : AprilTag tag36h11 family definition
                  (c) 2013-2016 The Regents of The University of Michigan
                  AprilRobotics/apriltag, BSD-2-Clause
                  Licence text: licenses/AprilTag-BSD-2-Clause.txt

      The 18 marker images were previously renderings credited to Nicola
      Castaman with no licence stated. They have been re-rendered from the
      published AprilTag family data (codewords and bit layout), which is
      BSD-2-Clause, so the images distributed here are this project's own output
      over permissively licensed data rather than someone else's unlicensed
      files.

      What the tags are, and that they are unchanged, is verified rather than
      asserted: each of the 18 images decodes to its own tag id with the
      reference AprilTag detector, and the module-level black/white pattern of
      every image is identical to the file it replaces. The two markers the
      simulation actually places in the world are tag36h11 ids 1 and 10, which
      is what the detector is configured to look for.

      The model.sdf, model.config and OGRE material scripts were rewritten as
      equivalent functional files for the same reason. Geometry (a 0.1 m square
      plane), material names and every file path are unchanged, so the world
      files and launch configuration are unaffected.

